          "reasoning_content": "We need to extract unverified occupational, executive, ownership, founder, board or trustee role proposals. The source entries mention a possible future CFO role for \"Voss\". The name candidate \"Voss\" (n3) is ambiguous, could refer to Luca or Leila. The text says \"If the acquisition closes, Voss will become chief financial officer of Juniper Energy in 2029; the notice does not specify which visitor and no appointment has occurred.\"\n\nWe need to output selection(s) with unique id, entry, first_token, last_token for the focus (the role title). The role title appears tokens 8-10: \"chief financial officer\". That's the focus. The statement_entry is entry 1. The focus is the role title phrase. The kind is role (since it's a role proposal). role_kind: executive (CFO). normalized: \"CFO\". subjects: we need to reference the person candidate(s). The text uses \"Voss\". The name candidate n3 (Voss) matches. But we cannot be sure which Voss, ambiguous. So we need subject_surface: selection id for the \"Voss\" token (token 5). We need a new selection for that surface. Also organization_surface: selection for \"Juniper Energy\" tokens 12-13. We need a new selection for that.\n\nState: hypothetical because conditional future appointment. status = hypothetical.\n\nBinding: is it direct? Both surfaces are exact text matching the candidate? Voss token matches candidate n3 text \"Voss\". The organization token \"Juniper Energy\" matches n2 text. So binding is direct.\n\nWe also need to include a Go-generated context selection per referenced entry? The instruction says \"Name candidates, new selections and one Go-generated context selection per referenced entry must total at most 64.\" Probably we need to create a selection for the role focus and for subject and organization surfaces. Also maybe a context selection for the entry? Not sure. The spec: \"Name candidates, new selections and one Go-generated context selection per referenced entry must total at most 64.\" So we might need to add a context selection per entry referenced (entry 1). Could be a selection covering whole entry? Probably not required ZERO? But they say must include one Go-generated context selection per referenced entry. So we need to add a selection (maybe id \"c0\") that selects the entire entry (or maybe a minimal token). We'll make a context selection covering the entry (maybe token 0-29). This selection is not used in interpretations but counts toward limit.\n\nNow we produce output JSON with \"selections\": list of selections (each with id, entry, first_token, last_token). Then \"interpretations\": list.\n\nWe need unique ids not using reserved ctx_ prefix. So selections ids like \"s0\",\"s1\",\"s2\",\"s3\". s0 for role focus (tokens 8-10). s1 for subject surface (token 5). s2 for organization surface (tokens 12-13). s3 for context selection for entry 1 (maybe token 0-29). For entry 0 maybe not referenced, but still it's not referenced by interpretation. Only referenced entry is 1. So we need one context selection for entry 1.\n\nInterpretation id maybe \"i0\". Provide fields: statement_entry: 1, focus: \"s0\", kind:\"role\", role_kind:\"executive\", normalized:\"CFO\", subjects:[\"n3\"], organizations:[\"n2\"], subject_surface:\"s1\", organization_surface:\"s2\", additional_evidence:[], binding:\"direct\", status:\"hypothetical\". Also maybe include \"additional_evidence\": [].\n\nWe also need context_links? none.\n\nNow generate."
